## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static portfolio site.

### What was implemented:

**Modified files:**
- `index.html` - Added Vercel Analytics CDN script tag

### Implementation details:

This project is a static HTML/JavaScript portfolio site without a build system or framework. After fetching the latest Vercel Analytics documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart, I determined the appropriate installation method for this architecture.

**Approach taken:**
- Used the CDN script method as recommended for static sites without bundlers
- Added `<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>` to the `<head>` section
- Placed just before the closing `</head>` tag to ensure it loads after other critical resources
- Used `defer` attribute for optimal page load performance

**Why this approach:**
1. The project has no build system (webpack, vite, etc.) - verified by checking for bundler config files
2. The existing JavaScript uses native ES6 modules but doesn't bundle npm packages
3. The CDN method is the official Vercel recommendation for static sites
4. This approach requires no dependencies or build process changes
5. The script automatically detects the Vercel deployment context and begins tracking

**Testing:**
- Verified the HTML serves correctly using Python's http.server
- Confirmed the analytics script tag is properly inserted in the HTML
- No build process to test as this is a static site served directly

**Next steps:**
Once deployed to Vercel, analytics will automatically start tracking:
- Page views
- User interactions
- Web Vitals metrics

The analytics data will be visible in the Vercel Dashboard under the Analytics tab after enabling Web Analytics in the project settings.
